Stdout:
[1mST108  Response violates schema[0m                                             [31mHIGH[0m
[2mchecks response_schema_conformance, response_headers_conformance   WFC 200[0m

A response body or header holds a value that its documented schema rejects.

[1mWhy it matters[0m
  Generated clients and typed SDKs trust the schema. A [36mnull[0m where the schema
  promises a string becomes a crash in the consumer's code, far from your API,
  with no hint of the cause. Every consumer who wrote code against the
  documented shape carries that bug.

[1mExample[0m
[2m  schema:[0m
    openapi: 3.0.3
    paths:
      /users/me:
        get:
          responses:
            '200':
              description: OK
              content:
                application/json:
                  schema:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      email:
                        type: string
[2m  response:[0m
    HTTP/1.1 200 OK
    Content-Type: application/json

    {"email": null}

[1mHow Schemathesis found it[0m
  Schemathesis validates the body against the schema for the response status and
  media type, and each documented header against its schema. The title names the
  part: [36mResponse violates schema[0m, [36mResponse header does not conform to the[0m
[36m  schema[0m, or an [36mSSE ...[0m title for Server-Sent Events.

  In the failure output for a body:

  - The first line names the violation, such as [36mnull is not of type "string"[0m.
  - [36mValidated against the response schema for status code 200.[0m names the
    response definition. A [36mdefault[0m or range match names that key instead.
  - [36mSchema at /properties/email:[0m gives the location in the schema and the
    subschema that failed.
  - [36mValue:[0m shows what the API returned.

[1mHow to fix[0m
  Decide which side is wrong.

  - The API is wrong: fix the serializer or the data. A [36mnull[0m points to a field
    your storage allows to be empty.
  - The schema is wrong: change it to match, for example [36mnullable: true[0m in
    OpenAPI 3.0. Widening the schema weakens what clients can rely on.

  Too many [36mformat[0m failures in bodies: set [36mvalidate-formats = false[0m under
  [36m[checks.response_schema_conformance][0m. Body format violations then go
  unreported, so turn it back on once you fix the structural failures. The
  setting leaves header formats checked.

[1mVerify the fix[0m
  Run [36mst replay <case id>[0m with the ID from the [36mTest Case ID:[0m line of the
  failure output. It reruns the stored case and reports whether it still fails;
  once it passes, replay deletes the stored case. The replay needs the run's
  credentials: run it with the same config, or pass [36m--header[0m, [36m--auth[0m or
  [36m--auth-wfc[0m.

[1mTurn it off[0m
  [36m--exclude-checks response_schema_conformance,response_headers_conformance[0m
  or in schemathesis.toml:
    [checks.response_schema_conformance]
    enabled = false
    [checks.response_headers_conformance]
    enabled = false
  Also disables:
    ST104  Missing Content-Type header
    ST107  Missing required headers
    ST109  JSON deserialization error
    ST110  Content deserialization error
    ST111  Discriminator value not in schema mapping

[1mDocs[0m  [4mhttps://schemathesis.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/failures/#st108[0m
